    "body": "This adds a test that passes on master and fails with the diff from #34618 applied, as davidgumberg asked in #34722. It covers both things that diff removes for a compact block more than two blocks ahead of the tip.\n\nIf the node already requested the block from this peer, it sends another `getdata` for the full block. Without that `getdata`, the block stays in flight from this peer and nothing requests it again until the block download timeout disconnects the peer. This check is the one shuv-amp proposed in #34722.\n\nOtherwise, from a high-bandwidth peer, the node handles the header as a headers message (`fRevertToHeaderProcessing`). Most of that work is done anyway. As 151henry151 pointed out in #34618, one part is not: protecting an outbound peer from eviction (`m_chain_sync.m_protect`). The test checks for the \"Protecting outbound peer\" debug log line.\n\nEach check fails when only its branch is disabled: `fRevertToHeaderProcessing = false` fails the protection check, and `if (false)` in place of `if (requested_block_from_this_peer)` makes the `getdata` check time out. shuv-amp first tested the two branches separately in #34618.\n\nFixes #34618.\n\n*Made with my usual tools: a computer, the Internet and an LLM. The mistakes, as usual, are all mine.*\n\n",
