      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree e221d63a61e2388608f5c324f932848cf0adb005\nparent aef8a04966d7ab6c04edc5d19b733e78205405de\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1790891895 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1791324288 +0200\n\ntest: cover compact blocks far ahead of the tip\n\nA compact block more than two blocks ahead of the tip is not\nreconstructed. If the node requested it from that peer, it asks for the\nfull block again. Otherwise it handles the header as a headers message\n(fRevertToHeaderProcessing). No test checked what either branch does,\nso removing both made no test fail.\n\nThe new test checks that the node sends a second getdata for a requested\nblock, and that an outbound high-bandwidth peer announcing such a block\nis protected from eviction. Only the headers path sets that protection.\n\nEach check fails if its branch in net_processing.cpp is disabled.\n",
